From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 08:58:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 21/71] docs: Add patch12, the hall and elevator patch series

patch12/ collects every change of the hall and elevator work as eight patches
that can be applied in order: the reconstructed iSentek IST8801 and Magnachip
MXM1120 hall switch drivers, the BBK elevator motor controller and its two
follow-up corrections (the vendor's move timings, states and key events, and
the attribute and module names), plus the three documentation commits that
carry the reverse engineering notes and the two full reports.

Its README records what each patch does, how to apply the series
(git am --keep-cr patch12/000*.patch, on top of the imported vendor tree), the
hardware facts recovered from the factory binary and device tree, the userspace
interface that has to stay identical, and - importantly - what the series does
not contain: the bbk_hall_core framework, the hall_ops registration in the two
sensor drivers, and the closed position loop of the elevator, whose
specification is complete in the reports but whose code is still to be written.

The series was verified by applying it to a worktree of the imported vendor tree
with git apply --check: all eight patches apply, and the resulting tree carries
the three drivers with the factory configuration unchanged, because the factory
config already enables all of the hall and elevator symbols.  An earlier patch
that "enabled" CONFIG_INPUT_IST8801 was dropped again: the factory config
already has that line, so it only added a duplicate.

