+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:33:55 +0800
+Subject: [PATCH] misc: Name the elevator driver like the vendor one
+
+Two naming details of the factory driver were missed and are part of the
+interface userspace sees:
+
+ - the frequency attribute is called vib_pwm_freq (the name string at
+   0x99f7617), not vib_pwm_frequency, so the path userspace opens is
+   .../vib_pwm_freq;
+ - the source file is gpio_pwm.c, so the module is called gpio_pwm and its
+   module parameters live under /sys/module/gpio_pwm/parameters/
+   (mhall_control_up, mhall_control_down and mhall_control2 to mhall_control7),
+   not under this driver's object name.
+
+The platform driver name stays bbk_vib_pwm and the sysfs directory stays
+soc:bbk_vib_pwm, as in the factory.  Renaming the file is what fixes the module
+parameter path, since KBUILD_MODNAME comes from the object name.
+
+Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
+---
