+
+s6patch霍尔/vib_pwm-逆向报告.md and s6patch霍尔/bbk_hall_core-逆向报告.md are
+the complete, instruction-level reverse engineering of the two remaining vendor
+drivers, and s6patch霍尔/README.md now records what they established.
+
+The vib_pwm report covers the 680 byte private structure field by field, the
+show and store of all fifteen sysfs attributes, the whole camera_state
+transition table including the intermediate and holder positions, the motor
+start and stop sequences, the three clock rates and how the nominal 19200 Hz
+durations are rescaled, the module parameter names and defaults, the key codes
+of the h110-vib-input device, and twenty ways a rewrite can go wrong.
+
+The bbk_hall_core report covers the misc device and its four ioctls, the layout
+of the two calibration files, the six sysfs attributes, the mhall_data
+structure, the exported API together with the hall_dev registration protocol,
+and the position interpolation between the five calibration anchors.
+
+The patch series that produces this work is tracked here as well.
+
