++++ b/s6patch霍尔/0005-misc-Match-the-vendor-elevator-driver-s-timings-stat.patch
+@@ -0,0 +1,1501 @@
++From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
++Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:06:59 +0800
++Subject: [PATCH] misc: Match the vendor elevator driver's timings, states and
++ key events
++
++A deeper disassembly of the factory gpio_pwm driver corrected several things in
++the first version of this rewrite:
++
++ - The move durations come from all_time (module parameter mhall_control7, 2839
++   by default) and not from fixed constants: a full travel takes all_time, the
++   69.6% position takes all_time * 696 / 1000, and moving between the two takes
++   the difference.  Every duration is then scaled by 6 / 10, the ratio between
++   the nominal 19200 Hz and the 32000 Hz a move actually runs at, before it is
++   handed to the hrtimer; durations above 65536 run a 50 ms preliminary stage
++   first and then the remainder at 41600 Hz scaled by 6 / 13.
++ - vib_pwm_camera_state has more states than 0, 1 and 2: 4 and 5 mean that a
++   move is running, 6 means the anti-pinch logic stopped the elevator and 7 is
++   the holder position between 1 and 2.  Finishing a move must write the target
++   into camera_state, otherwise the busy test (state & ~1) == 4 refuses every
++   later request.
++ - vib_pwm_enable takes 1 for up and 2 for down, and any other value only
++   brakes the driver; it does not touch the move state or the timer.
++ - vib_pwm_time treats 1300 as "all_time plus ten", not as a literal duration.
++ - The show strings are part of the interface: vib_id=%d, vib_freq=%d,
++   count=%d, enable=%d, dir=%d, time=%d all_time=%d, and clear_cali_data
++   reports the constant "clear".
++ - vib_pwm_abort_notify is a keyword protocol, not a number: the camera stack
++   writes "0x27c"/"636", "0x27d"/"637", "0x27f"/"639", "0x280"/"640",
++   "0x282"/"642", "0x283"/"643", "0x284"/"644", "666", "888", "stream on",
++   "stream off", "username:" and "com.eebbk.askhomework", and each one triggers
++   its own elevator command, key event or restart of the current mode.
++ - The driver also registers the input device h110-vib-input (phys
++   h110-vib/input0, bus type 0x19) and injects keys 635 to 646, one press and
++   one release per event.  The camera stack watches those, so leaving them out
++   would leave the elevator mechanically working but invisible to userspace.
++ - The gpio sequence, the clock handling and the state machine run under the
++   driver lock, and the timer callback no longer tries to cancel its own timer,
++   which would spin forever in hrtimer_cancel().
++ - The module parameters mhall_control_up, _down and 2 to 7 are provided with
++   the factory names, permissions and default values.
++ - The private data is zeroed, where the vendor left enable, target_state,
++   holder_mode, all_count and notify_str uninitialised.
++
++The two reverse engineering reports that back this up are added by the next
++commit.
++
++Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
